    <h3>1. The service</h3>
    <p>FirmLedger is a public business directory and record ledger. It lets anyone browse canonical business profiles and lets registered users submit new records, claim ownership of records through domain verification, manage records they own, and request corrections or removals.</p>

    <h3>2. Eligibility and accounts</h3>
    <p>You must be at least 18 and able to form a binding contract to hold an account. You must register with a valid email you control, keep your password secret, and be responsible for everything that happens under your account. One person should operate one account. We may suspend or delete accounts that violate these terms; suspended users cannot sign in, and their sessions expire immediately.</p>

    <h3>3. Your content and accuracy duties</h3>
    <p>When you submit a record, timeline event, source or relationship, you represent that the content is, to the best of your knowledge, accurate and current; that you have the right to submit it; and that it does not infringe any third party's rights. You must not submit deliberately false facts, fabricate sources, impersonate another entity, mentor or owner, or misdescribe a business's owner, revenue, size or status. Moderation review is not a substitute for these duties — you remain responsible for what you submit.</p>

    <h3>4. Moderation</h3>
    <p>All submissions pass human review before publication. We may approve, edit, request changes to, or reject any content at our discretion; we may unpublish, correct, or remove existing records (including via the public removal-request process) at any time, and we may do so without prior notice where accuracy, safety or legality requires.</p>

    <h3>5. Ownership claims and verification</h3>
    <p>Claiming a record requires cryptographic proof that you control the record's official domain — a DNS TXT record, an HTML meta tag, or the FirmLedger badge. You must only start a claim for a business you are actually authorized to represent. Fraudulent claiming (including impersonation, doctored screenshots, or DNS takeovers) is a material breach of these terms and may expose you to legal liability; we will reverse such claims and suspend the accounts involved. A verified owner must keep the verification proof in place; removing it may revert the record to unclaimed status.</p>

    <h3>6. The badge</h3>
    <p>The FirmLedger badge is licensed for use solely on the verified owner's own website, linked to the owner's FirmLedger profile, unmodified, and in a way that does not imply endorsement of claims not on the profile. You may not use it on any other site, to imply a partnership with FirmLedger, or in a broken/cached form that shows status you no longer hold.</p>

    <h3>7. Acceptable use</h3>
    <p>You may not: scrape the site in bulk or in a way that degrades the service (rate limits apply); attempt unauthorized access or probing; use the site to send spam; upload malware; abuse the directory for SEO spam (low-effort, keyword-stuffed records will be rejected); index or republish the corpus commercially without a data licence; or use it in any way unlawful in your jurisdiction or in Kenya.</p>
    <p>Fair-use crawling is welcomed: <code>robots.txt</code> and the sitemap index define canonical access; retrieving public pages for personal research, journalism or reference is fine.</p>

    <h3>8. Intellectual property</h3>
    <p>Business names, logos and trademarks remain the property of the respective owners. Descriptions and articles you read on FirmLedger may contain material sourced from Wikipedia and Wikidata (content available under CC BY-SA, attribution maintained in the Sources section of each profile). The FirmLedger compilation — structure, schema, scoring, design and software — is ours, © FirmLedger 2026.</p>

    <h3>9. No warranty; limits of liability</h3>
    <p>The directory is provided "as is". Records are moderated and where possible cited, but we make no warranty — express or implied — of accuracy, completeness, suitability for investment or credit decisions, or fitness for any purpose. Verification signals ("Verified owner", confidence scores, tech detection) are technical readings made at a point in time, not guarantees of good faith. To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential damages, lost profits, or business decisions made in reliance on the directory; aggregate liability is capped at the greater of USD 100 or the amounts you paid us in the past 12 months (currently zero, as the service is free).</p>

    <h3>10. Changes</h3>
    <p>We may revise these terms from time to time; material changes will be posted on this page with a revised effective date. Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance.</p>

    <h3>11. Governing law</h3>
